---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white mb-4">
        About This Journey
      </h1>
      <p class="text-text-muted text-lg">
        Documenting the process, not just the result.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert prose-brand max-w-none">
      <h2>Goal</h2>
      <p>
        The purpose of this website is to serve as a personal knowledge base and public ledger of my cybersecurity studies. Learning complex technical subjects is an iterative process, and writing about them helps solidify understanding.
      </p>

      <h2>Current Focus</h2>
      <p>
        I am currently focusing on understanding the fundamentals of systems and networking, before diving deeper into web application security and penetration testing methodologies.
      </p>
      
      <ul>
        <li>Web Security Fundamentals (OWASP Top 10)</li>
        <li>Network Protocols & Architecture</li>
        <li>Linux Administration & Privilege Escalation</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Philosophy</h2>
      <blockquote>
        "The only true wisdom is in knowing you know nothing." - Socrates
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        Security is a massive domain. This site isn't meant to be a definitive guide for others, but rather a reflection of my current understanding, which will inevitably evolve, be corrected, and expand over time.
      </p>

      <h2>Tools</h2>
      <p>
        This site is statically generated using <strong>Astro</strong>, styled with <strong>Tailwind CSS</strong>, and deployed via <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>. The content is written entirely in Markdown, ensuring a frictionless authoring experience.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
